 ## StartPlasma
 
-`startplasma` is the main binary invoked by the login manager. It is compiled as two binaries (`startplasma-x11` and `startplasma-wayland`) with some common files. It sets up key environment variables and other core GUI-less tasks, and then triggers the main startup sequence either via requesting the plasma systemd target, or a legacy fallback via plasma-session.
+`startplasma` is the main binary invoked by the login manager. It is compiled as two binaries (`startplasma-x11` and `startplasma-nwin`) with some common files. It sets up key environment variables and other core GUI-less tasks, and then triggers the main startup sequence either via requesting the plasma systemd target, or a legacy fallback via plasma-session.
 
-`startplasma` tracks the status of ksmserver (x11) or kwin_wayland (wayland) to detect when to exit. To ensure all shutdown tasks are complete, it also waits until `plasma-shutdown` exits.
+The installed `plasma-nwin.desktop` login entry is **Plasma (NWin)**. It executes the compiled `startplasma-nwin`, not an old compositor startup shim. The Wayland target requires and binds to `plasma-nwin_wayland.service`, and startup watches `org.kde.NWinWrapper` to detect session exit. The non-systemd path launches `nwin_wayland_wrapper` directly. X11 startup remains backed by the separately installed external KWin X11.
+
+To ensure all shutdown tasks are complete, startup also waits until `plasma-shutdown` exits. Native Wayland session IPC uses `org.kde.NWin.Session` on `/Session`; the X11 session retains its external KWin interface.
+
+Bundled IPC clients use `org.kde.NWin` and `/NWin` for native compositor controls. Actual Wayland compositor settings use `nwinrc`; look-and-feel packages retain their existing `[kwinrc]` theme metadata schema and apply those values to the session's compositor config. Published Wayland protocol names remain unchanged.
+
+The native session publishes `XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=NWin:KDE` (`DesktopNames=NWin;KDE`) so portal selection uses the separately installed native NWin backend while retaining KDE desktop recognition. X11 continues to publish `KDE` and use the stock KDE portal backend.
 
